+## 4. `vitaFTPShell`
+
+### Status
+
+`planning`. There is no source tree, CMake project, or VPK yet. The strategy is
+[`vitaFTPShell/STRATEGY.md`](../vitaFTPShell/STRATEGY.md).
+
+The product is one console app that is both an FTP client and a local file
+manager: local and remote are two live panes, and moving a file is one action.
+The user is the anonymous-first collector pulling homebrew and media from saved
+public FTP sites, with logins kept for sites that need them.
+
+Server mode is a compatibility surface, not the core bet. It exists so
+VitaShell users need one app instead of two, and it shares the same protocol
+engine.
+
+### Constraints already decided
+
+- Plain FTP only in v1; no SFTP or FTPS.
+- No background daemon or taiHEN system plugin; transfers end with the app.
+- No PC-first workflow and no desktop-client port.
+- No VitaShell feature-parity race.
+- GPLv3, because the local file manager builds on VitaShell. This project is an
+  island inside the MIT workspace; do not copy its code into the MIT projects.
+
