+## D103 — CORE reports system CPU load from the userland scheduler counters
+
+**Status:** Accepted (2026-11-08; supersedes D6)
+**Context:** D6 concluded that no userland API reports system-wide CPU utilisation and rejected idle-time sampling as measuring only this process. That premise was wrong. `sceKernelGetSystemInfo()` is a normal `SceLibKernel` export: `SceKernelSystemInfo` carries a cumulative idle clock, a wakeup count, and a thread-switch count for each of the four cores. PSVshell derives per-core load from the idle-clock delta over a microsecond tick; the same calculation works from userland without a plugin. CORE had lost its ARM/GPU/BUS rows in D99 and was left with memory only, which made the hero panel answer a narrower question than the machine it describes.
+**Decision:** CORE shows four per-core CPU percentages, their active-core average, and context-switch/wakeup rates per second. The 20 s trace becomes aggregate CPU load on a fixed 0–100 % axis; the three memory pools stay as the second row. The platform adapter returns raw counters (`idle_us`, `time_us`, cumulative switches/wakeups, active mask); `core/metrics.c` owns the delta and percentage policy. A core outside `activeCpuMask` renders `--`, not 0 %. If an idle delta exceeds the elapsed time, the sample is refused and the panel renders `--`, so a unit mismatch cannot become a fabricated percentage. The applied ARM/GPU/BUS clocks remain omitted: the userland ScePower getters return this process's request, not the machine's value. GPU work is represented by the CDRAM/PHY pools and the pinned FRAME strip; there is no GPU-load or applied-GPU-clock API in userland.
+**Consequence:** The hero panel answers "what is the machine doing, and how much memory is left?" with real system data. It adds no plugin, no boot surface, and no new import outside `SceLibKernel` (already linked). `sceKernelGetSystemInfo` and the microseconds interpretation of `idleClock` are `[C]` until a console run confirms them; a failure degrades to `--` rather than a wrong number.
+**Rejected:** keeping the memory-only panel; a kernel plugin or bridge for clocks; printing the ScePower request as `REQ`; deriving CPU load from this process's run time; a fabricated GPU load or `GPU CLK N/A` row; an autoscaling CPU trace that would make 5 % look like 95 %.
+**Verification:** `[V]` host tests cover per-core percentages, the active mask, the aggregate, the rates, a delta larger than elapsed time failing closed, a failed read leaving the trace alone, and the fixed-scale trace. `[C]` `sceKernelGetSystemInfo` availability and `idleClock` units on 3.65 Enso are unconfirmed until the b153 console run.
